    "vesting": "Vesting date = the calendar day after the last day of the applicable period (spec A3).",
    "working_days": "Mon-Fri excluding 5 U.S.C. 6103 federal holidays (spec A2: 'working days' is undefined in part 435). 2026-09-07 (Labor Day) and 2026-10-12 (Columbus Day) are holidays. Counting starts the day after the vesting date (spec A6); the deadline is for the refund being SENT (435.1(b)).",
    "shipment": "Shipment = first carrier-possession event. 'Label created' is not shipment.",
    "deadline_meaning": "Computed deadlines are the SELLER's prompt-refund deadline (tracking/escalation). If paid by consumer credit card, R03's own 60-day notice clock runs independently.",
    "outcome_vocabulary": [
      "eligible",
      "likely_eligible_missing_evidence",
      "possible_contract_benefit",
      "needs_facts",
      "manual_review",
      "not_eligible",
      "deadline_passed",
      "source_unverified",
      "unsupported",
      "not_yet_due"
    ],
    "loader": "A case has EITHER a top-level `expected` OR an `expected` on every variant. `clock` (and optional `source`) may be set on the case or on a variant; a variant value overrides the case value. `facts_from: <case id>` + `facts_override: {...}` means: copy that case's facts, then replace the named facts. A variant's `change` object replaces the named facts for that variant only. Every `facts` value is an object; no prose placeholders.",
    "fact_states": "user_confirmed | observed | derived | extracted_candidate | conflicting | missing | assumption. Contract §2.5 mapping: user_confirmed→confirmed, observed→observed, derived→derived, extracted_candidate→candidate, conflicting→conflicting, missing→missing (value null), assumption→assumption-class candidate. D147(2)/X1: `eligible` requires every decisive fact to be user_confirmed, or observed/derived from confirmed facts; an extracted_candidate decisive fact caps the outcome at likely_eligible_missing_evidence (the case lists it in expected.unconfirmed_decisive_facts). Since M2D the baseline cases use user_confirmed for decisive facts (the state after the user's fact review); each file has explicit cap variants.",
    "conflicting": "D152/D154 (README cross-pack rule 3): conflict_kind 'candidates' → different outcomes or amounts = needs_facts; same outcome and amount = capped at likely_eligible_missing_evidence (fact listed in unconfirmed_decisive_facts). conflict_kind 'confirmed_vs_observed' / 'confirmed_vs_confirmed' → manual_review. A conflicting or extracted-only deadline anchor never gives a firm date: deadline.date = null, status disputed_anchor / unknown_anchor, and (user-obligor paths only) advisory_act_by from the earliest candidate.",
    "not_yet_due": "D147(6)/X3: a path that is not ripe yet has outcome not_yet_due with expected.reevaluate_at (ISO date) or expected.reevaluate_when (event); never not_eligible.",
    "missing_source": "X5: a variant with source.record = 'missing' means no current source record exists for the pack → source_unverified.",
    "calendar_zone": "Calendar days are the buyer's local dates at the ship-to address (spec A5); fixtures use America/New_York (-04:00) unless stated."
  },
